{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_BmAaiJWL0xi1gS3bcMccg7OE","name":"get_story","input":{"id":18},"output":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":18,\"title\":\"Break work down in the Shortcut Way\",\"state\":\"To Do\",\"story_type\":\"chore\",\"team\":\"Walid Hl's Team\",\"owners\":[],\"requester\":\"walidhl\",\"due_date\":\"2026-08-21T04:00:00Z\",\"description\":\"![stories.png](https://static.shortcut.com/images/onboarding/stories.png)\\n\\n### 🎟️ Stories represent a shippable scope of customer value\\n- Capture the problem that needs solving, and specify requirements\\n- Features, Bugs, and Chores are all types of Stories\\n\\n### ✔️ Sub-tasks capture the implementation steps of Stories\\n- Aim to break down a Story into Sub-tasks that can be completed in a few days\\n- Sub-tasks should enable parallel work when possible and minimize dependencies\\n\\n### 🏁 Epics are groups of related Stories that deliver a larger outcome\\n- Keep Epics scoped to deliver value within a timeframe (a week, month, quarter)\\n- Include clear success criteria and measurable objectives to learn from what you ship\\n---\\n\\n### 💡 Separate business value from the implementation work\\nStories and Epics should capture _what_ we want to accomplish, where Sub-tasks should capture _how_ it is accomplished.\\n\\n---\",\"tasks\":[],\"comments\":[],\"story_links\":[]}"}]},"is_error":false,"at":"2026-08-18T21:43:26.870Z"}
